<title>USA: GM's fourth quarter income slashed by strikes.</title>
<headline>GM's fourth quarter income slashed by strikes.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp. Tuesday reported fourth quarter income of $786 million, less than half of the $1.87 billion it earned a year ago, as labor woes in the United States and Canada took $700 million out of profits.</p>
<p>The world's largest automaker said it earned 92 cents a share, down from $1.98 a year earlier. Revenue fell to $40.9 billion from $41.4 billion.</p>
